<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11696" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crŭcĭābĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		crucio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>tormenting, torturing, painful, excruciating,
				miserable</i> (rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not in Cic.): cruciabilem me accipito,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 4, 1, 40</span></i>
			 Ritschl: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exitu periit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					3, 9, 7</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mors,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. adv. Gent. 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silentio fatigatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 239, 20</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Susceptible of torture</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 7, 20, 9</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crŭcĭābĭlĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>with torture</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps.
				4, 1, 40</span></i> Fleck., Lorenz: interfecti, Auct. B. Afr.
		46.</div>
